## Architecture Improvements

### Path Resolution Flow

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Application Starts] --> B{PCP_DATA_DIR env set?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Use PCP_DATA_DIR]
    B -->|No| D{ProgramData exists + writable?}
    D -->|Yes| E[Use ProgramData]
    D -->|No| F{LocalAppData writable?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Use LocalAppData]
    F -->|No| H[Use User Profile]
    
    C --> I[Create config/logs/db/temp]
    E --> I
    G --> I
    H --> I
    
    I --> J{Output path from config valid?}
    J -->|Yes| K[Use configured path]
    J -->|No| L[Fallback to Documents\PCP_Output]
    L --> M[Auto-update config]
```

### Threading Model

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[UI Thread] -->|Log Queue| B[Console Display]
    C[Engine Thread] -->|Log Queue| B
    D[Worker Threads] -->|Log Queue| B
    
    A -->|root.after| E[UI Updates]
    D -->|root.after| E
    
    F[Test Connection Button] --> G[Worker Thread]
    G -->|COM Initialize| H[Outlook API]
    G -->|root.after| I[Update Dropdowns]
    
    J[Open Dashboard Button] --> K[Worker Thread]
    K -->|Generate HTML| L[Dashboard Generator]
    K -->|root.after| M[Open Browser]
```

---

## Key Takeaways

1. **Path Management:** Never hardcode paths. Always use platform-appropriate fallback logic.

2. **UI Threading:** All long-running operations (I/O, COM, network) MUST run in worker threads. UI updates MUST use `root.after()`.

3. **COM Threading:** `pythoncom.CoInitialize()` must be called in EACH worker thread that uses COM, never in the UI thread.

4. **Error Recovery:** Validate all external inputs (config paths, folder names) and provide automatic fallbacks.

5. **Console Performance:** Bound log processing per tick and trim old lines to prevent UI slowdown.

